.TH S3AR-COPY 1 "September 2026" "s3ar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
s3ar-copy \- copy one S3 object on the server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s3ar-copy
.RB [ \-v | \-vv | \-vvv ]
.RB [ \-\-create-bucket ]
.RB [ \-\-multipart-size " SIZE" ]
.I s3://SOURCE_BUCKET/SOURCE_KEY s3://DESTINATION_BUCKET/DESTINATION_KEY
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B s3ar-copy
copies one object using S3 multipart copy. Object data does not pass through
the client. An empty object uses CopyObject. An existing destination key is
overwritten. Source and destination must differ.
.PP
The source is checked with HEAD. Each copied part uses the source ETag as a
condition; if the source changes, copying stops. User metadata, content type,
content encoding, and cache control are applied to the destination. ACL and
server-side encryption settings are determined by the destination bucket.
.PP
Keys are literal, not URL-decoded. A trailing slash is part of a key. Quote
operands containing spaces or shell metacharacters.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-create-bucket
Create the destination bucket if it does not exist.
.TP
.BI \-\-multipart-size " SIZE"
Set the part size. SIZE must be between 5M and 5G, inclusive, with binary
suffix M or G. The default is 16M. At most 10,000 parts are allowed.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity. Repeat twice for debug messages or three times for HTTP
trace. Further repetitions have no effect.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command usage on standard output and exit successfully.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Increase diagnostic verbosity by one level.
.TP
.B SIGUSR2
Decrease diagnostic verbosity by one level.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR S3AR_ENDPOINT ,
.BR S3AR_REGION ,
.BR S3AR_URI_STYLE ,
.BR S3AR_ACCESS_KEY ,
.BR S3AR_SECRET_KEY ,
and
.B S3AR_SESSION_TOKEN
configure the S3 connection as for
.BR s3ar (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The copy or help completed successfully.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments, configuration error, or S3 failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3ar (1),
.BR s3ar-delete (1),
.BR s3ar-get (1),
.BR s3ar-list (1),
.BR s3ar-put (1)
